<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title><%= title %> — <%= appName %></title>
  <%- include('../_style') %>
</head>
<body>
  <div class="wrap">
    <h1><%= title %></h1>
    <p class="muted">Last updated <%= updatedAt %></p>

    <h2>Using the app</h2>
    <p class="meaning">
      HariHariBol is offered for personal devotional use. You need an account, created through
      Google or Apple sign-in, and you are responsible for what happens under it.
    </p>

    <h2>What is free</h2>
    <p class="meaning">
      The books, verses, translations, mantras, chanting, sadhana tracking and the daily
      sloka are free. Premium adds the mood-driven sloka — reporting what you are struggling
      with and receiving a verse chosen for it.
    </p>

    <h2>Premium and donations</h2>
    <p class="meaning">
      Premium is a monthly subscription. It is also granted permanently to anyone who donates
      any amount, through Google Play, Apple or Razorpay.
    </p>
    <p class="meaning">
      Subscriptions renew automatically until cancelled. Cancel through the store you bought
      it from; access continues to the end of the period you have already paid for. Refunds
      are handled by the store under its own policy.
    </p>

    <h2>Content</h2>
    <p class="meaning">
      Scripture, translations and commentary are reproduced from their sources and remain the
      property of their respective authors and publishers. They are provided for personal
      devotional study, not for redistribution.
    </p>

    <h2>Explanations written by the app</h2>
    <p class="meaning">
      Some short notes in the app are written by us or generated with AI assistance. These are
      always presented separately from acharya commentary and are never attributed to any
      teacher. If something reads as though it were, that is a bug — please report it.
    </p>

    <h2>Ending an account</h2>
    <p class="meaning">
      You can delete your account at any time from within the app. We may suspend an account
      that is used to abuse the service or other users.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p class="meaning">
      <a href="mailto:support@hariharibol.com">support@hariharibol.com</a>
    </p>

    <footer class="muted"><p><%= appName %> &middot; <%= year %></p></footer>
  </div>
</body>
</html>
